### Streaming vs Single-Turn Mode

The SDK always streams messages. Process them in a loop:

```typescript
// TypeScript
for await (const message of query(...)) {
  // Each message arrives as it's generated
  console.log(message);
}
```

```python
# Python
async for message in query(...):
    # Each message arrives as it's generated
    print(message)
```

### Permission Modes

| Mode | Behavior | Use Case |
|------|----------|----------|
| `default` | Requests permission for each tool | Interactive workflows |
| `acceptEdits` | Auto-approves file operations | Trusted development |
| `bypassPermissions` | No permission checks (auto-approve all) | CI/CD pipelines |
| `plan` | Planning mode (read-only) | Pre-execution review |

